Day 08 of my bug bounty series: working with Burp Suite.

I set it up on Day 03. Today I actually learned to use it.

4 parts I spent time on:

1. Proxy: intercept and inspect requests between browser and server.
2. Repeater: change a request, resend it, and watch how the app responds.
3. Target: a map of the application's pages and endpoints.
4. HTTP history: every captured request and response, ready to review.

Burp doesn't find bugs by itself. It shows you what the app is really doing.

